Expected elements: present

Every must-show item is here and no must-not-show item is: identity bar with chain exit, both stepping directions, scrubber, 128/1315 readout, phase rail; Code positioned at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as one tabbed region, Call Trace open, seven frames; Values a separate pane below with ten values; the `Data` row with its `Synthetic demo data` badge leading the Transaction pane. A dense, scannable surface.

Change (a) reads as continuation, and the fade is conditional, which is the part that matters: Code ghosts row 52 below line 51, Transaction dims into the EXECUTIONS sentence, while Values (content ends 23px above its floor) and Call Trace (229px above) carry none. Neither will read as clipped now.

Standing observation, measured here: Call Trace body y95–558, content ends y328 — **229px empty of 463px, 49.5%**. It holds, matching laptop/light's 48.8%. But Values has only ~8% slack here, so height cannot be re-weighted inside the middle column; the starved pane, Transaction, is in column three, is also the loosest (30.5px rows against Values' 25px), and spends four lines on two unwrapped 66-char hashes with 2-char orphans. Tightening it recovers ~150px — enough to lift the humanised EXECUTIONS sentence and the Selector/Raw rows, currently unverifiable below the fade, into view.

Top fixes: tighten and truncate the Transaction pane; treat the Code pane's right edge, which still hard-clips mid-token.

Rating: 7/10

